coder › Done. Implemented both functions in `src/query.ts` and added a test suite in `src/query.test.ts`, on branch `work/query-parse-stringify` (commit `f03d978`).

## What changed

**`src/query.ts`**
- `parseQuery(text)` — strips one leading `?`; empty input returns `{}`; splits on `&`; each segment is split on its first `=` (a segment with no `=` gives value `''`); keys and values are decoded via `decodeComponent` (`+` → space, then `decodeURIComponent`); values accumulate per key and a key seen once becomes a string, more than once an ordered array. Empty segments (e.g. from a trailing `&`) are skipped.
- `stringifyQuery(query)` — walks keys in insertion order; arrays emit one `key=value` pair per element; both keys and values go through `encodeURIComponent`, which encodes spaces as `%20` (no `+`); an empty-string value serializes as `key=`; no leading `?`.

**`src/query.test.ts`** — 14 tests covering single vs. repeated keys, keys without `=`, leading `?`, percent-decoding and `+`-as-space, empty-string input, insertion order, one-pair-per-array-value, `%20` for spaces, key encoding, empty-string values, and two round trips (object → string → object, and string → object → string) including string and array values.

